# Optional. build.sh can compose this from the environment instead, which keeps
# secrets off your disk entirely — see autograder/build.sh header:
#
#   ORALSCALE_SECRET=$(node ../tools/make-config.js --print) \
#     GENAI_STUDIO_API_KEY=sk-... bash build.sh
#
# If you do keep this file, it is gitignored and build.sh chmod 600s it.
# NOTE: whatever is here ends up INSIDE autograder.zip in plaintext — Gradescope
# has no secrets manager. Treat the zip like a password.

ORALSCALE_SECRET=your-signing-secret-here     # MUST match the Signer's secret
ORALSCALE_WEBAPP_URL=https://your-app.pages.dev/
ORALSCALE_MAX_POINTS=10

# ORALSCALE_ASSIGNMENT is OPTIONAL and best left unset: without it the week is
# read from the Gradescope assignment title, so ONE zip serves every week.
# Set it only to pin this zip to a single assignment id from course.json.
# ORALSCALE_ASSIGNMENT=week-04-methods-core

# --- Purdue GenAI Studio (optional; deterministic heuristic fallback if omitted) ---
# Use a DEDICATED, revocable key — not your personal all-purpose one — and rotate
# it at end of term. Anyone with Gradescope staff access can read it.
# GENAI_STUDIO_API_KEY=sk-...
# GENAI_STUDIO_BASE_URL=https://genai.rcac.purdue.edu
# GENAI_STUDIO_MODEL=...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instructor notification (accommodation review only). OFF BY DEFAULT.
#
# ⚠️ Deliberately off pending a records-policy decision, not merely unconfigured.
# Mailing an accommodation review hands an outside mail provider the fact that a
# particular Gradescope submission needs looking at for accommodation reasons.
# Even carrying no student name, that leaves the institutional boundary the rest
# of this system keeps student work inside, and whether it is acceptable is a
# question for your institution rather than a default this code should pick.
#
# With it off, an unverifiable accommodation is still flagged in the
# instructor-only tests on the submission itself, inside Gradescope. The email
# only makes it easier to notice.
#
# To turn it on you must set ORALSCALE_NOTIFY_ENABLED=1 as well as the SMTP
# settings — leaving credentials here is deliberately NOT enough to start
# sending.
#
# When a student selects an extended-time accommodation that cannot be verified
# automatically, the submission is GRADED NORMALLY and you get an email telling
# you to look at it. Without this configured nothing breaks — the flag still
# appears in the submission's instructor-only tests — but you would have to go
# looking for it, which for one submission in two hundred means never.
#
# The email deliberately carries NO student name, identifier, or accommodation
# detail: only the assignment and the Gradescope submission id. It is a pointer,
# not a copy. Disability information stays inside Gradescope (INV-ACCOM-3).
#
# Deliverability from a Gradescope container is not guaranteed — outbound SMTP
# may be blocked. Send yourself a test submission before relying on it.
# ORALSCALE_NOTIFY_ENABLED=1
# ORALSCALE_NOTIFY_TO=you@purdue.edu
# ORALSCALE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.edu
# ORALSCALE_SMTP_PORT=587
# ORALSCALE_SMTP_USER=
# ORALSCALE_SMTP_PASS=
# ORALSCALE_SMTP_FROM=
